> It is a well-known fact that when you *continue* eating a corpse you
> started on when you weren't satiated, you won't die by overeating, even
> when you're satiated when you continue eating.
> 
> Will this also work if you ate something in between?

No. Starting to eat something else (or, for that matter, saving and
restoring), resets the game's memory of the previous bit of food,
including the information whether it was exempting you from choking
because of original non-satiation. (victual.canchoke in eat.c)

